<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhagwan Rao of Datia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhagwan Rao was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vir-singh-deo">Bir Singh Deo of Orchha</a>, who received Datia in 1626 and founded it as a separate state. His father had already built the great seven-storey palace at Datia. His descendants ruled Datia as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> until the state merged into independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
